WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.223
My name is Zhang Mei Jin, and I am a 22-year-old silk worker living in Guangdong Province, China.

2
00:00:07.224 --> 00:00:13.098
The year is 1880 and China trades many goods worldwide, especially silk.

3
00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:19.796
Part of the Pearl River Delta is located here, which makes this area one of China’s most important sources of silk.

4
00:00:19.797 --> 00:00:25.612
The river is rich with sand and mud, and this material fertilizes the mulberry trees.

5
00:00:25.613 --> 00:00:29.889
We use mulberry leaves to feed the silkworms that produce the silk.

6
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:35.326
Most of the women in my village work in the silk industry, including my grandmother and mother,

7
00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:39.222
and our expertise has given us more power and independence.

8
00:00:39.223 --> 00:00:44.779
After all, without the women silk workers, how can our village survive?

9
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:51.392
Chinese silk has been regarded as the best in the world for many centuries and is in high demand.

10
00:00:51.393 --> 00:00:53.671
Perhaps you know of the Silk Road?

11
00:00:53.672 --> 00:01:02.795
The Silk Road allowed our ancestors to trade many different types of goods with foreign merchants, but silk was always China’s main commodity.

12
00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:06.668
So China guarded the secret of its silk carefully.

13
00:01:06.669 --> 00:01:14.342
Taking a silkworm out of China was forbidden, but many foreigners still tried to obtain our precious Chinese silkworms.

14
00:01:14.343 --> 00:01:19.153
Long ago the ones who tried to smuggle silkworms out of the country were executed,

15
00:01:19.154 --> 00:01:25.048
so it was many centuries before anyone learned the secret of Chinese silk.

16
00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:33.474
A silkworm is a caterpillar, and when this caterpillar becomes an adult moth, the female lays three hundred to five hundred eggs.

17
00:01:33.475 --> 00:01:40.154
These eggs are so tiny that 35,000 of them weigh only 28 grams.

18
00:01:40.155 --> 00:01:50.527
As soon as the eggs hatch, the young silkworms are placed on wooden trays, and these trays are stacked on top of each other inside a dry farmhouse.

19
00:01:50.528 --> 00:01:56.372
Fresh, shredded mulberry leaves are sprinkled on top of the young worms, and they eat and eat.

20
00:01:56.373 --> 00:02:03.343
When I was seven years old, my job was to help pick leaves from the mulberry trees and fill many baskets with them.

21
00:02:03.344 --> 00:02:12.318
My mother and the other women feed the silkworms every two hours, day and night, and all you hear are worms crunching on the leaves.

22
00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:14.993
The farm is quite noisy!

23
00:02:14.994 --> 00:02:19.675
The work is very hard because each worm has to be put on a new,

24
00:02:19.676 --> 00:02:26.804
clean tray every day and needs to be protected from bright light, loud noises, and strong smells.

25
00:02:26.805 --> 00:02:36.397
The worms don’t like to be disturbed or they don’t grow well, and when I was a young girl, my mother never let me even speak inside the farmhouse.

26
00:02:36.398 --> 00:02:40.786
This was difficult because I had so many questions to ask!

27
00:02:40.787 --> 00:02:49.122
After about a month of eating, resting, and shedding their skin four times, the silkworms are ready to spin their cocoons.

28
00:02:49.123 --> 00:02:58.373
This is when the workers put them on spinning racks, and the silkworm builds its cocoon by making a long fiber and surrounding itself with it.

29
00:02:58.374 --> 00:03:02.659
In about three days, the silkworms look like white balls.

30
00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:09.769
Then, eight to ten days later, the cocoons are ready to be unwound, a process called reeling.

31
00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:14.660
Right now I am still being trained by one of my aunts to unwind the cocoons.

32
00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:21.771
My job is to reel the silk threads onto a large spinning wheel, but we have a machine that helps us to do this.

33
00:03:21.772 --> 00:03:30.235
Our reeling machine is built directly over a large pot of very hot water, and I put the cocoons in the pot to kill the worms inside.

34
00:03:30.236 --> 00:03:39.467
A long wooden plank, placed across the pot, has two poles that have two small rollers attached, and a bamboo tube hangs from each roller.

35
00:03:39.468 --> 00:03:44.761
As I stir the cocoons in the hot water, the ends of the silk fibers float free.

36
00:03:44.762 --> 00:03:53.027
I grab the ends of the threads, gently pull and twist them together, and feed these fibers through the bamboo tube.

37
00:03:53.028 --> 00:03:58.319
Then the fibers wind around the rollers and onto a large reeling wheel.

38
00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:04.607
When the fiber of the cocoon is completely unwound, only the dead insect is left.

39
00:04:04.608 --> 00:04:11.688
Silk reeling is very tricky, and it takes years of experience to learn how to do it just right.

40
00:04:11.689 --> 00:04:19.388
One silkworm can make a strand of silk about one thousand meters long—the longer the strand, the better the silk.

41
00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:23.471
If a strand is too short, the quality of the silk suffers.

42
00:04:23.472 --> 00:04:30.506
Remember, the best-quality silk thread is one that is reeled continuously in one long strand,

43
00:04:30.507 --> 00:04:34.565
which means I cannot break the fragile thread as I am handling it.

44
00:04:34.566 --> 00:04:39.674
I have heard that automatic machines powered by steam are being used now

45
00:04:39.675 --> 00:04:45.179
because they can reel many cocoons at a time and unwind the silk more quickly.

46
00:04:45.193 --> 00:04:51.450
Businessmen are building large factories near cities and employing hundreds of women to work in them.

47
00:04:51.451 --> 00:04:58.017
But these factories are very noisy and some silk workers have gotten injured using the machines.

48
00:04:58.018 --> 00:05:02.978
Many of our friends and neighbors have left our village to find work in the factories.

49
00:05:02.979 --> 00:05:13.454
We miss them, but my family is content to stay here and stick to the older traditions because we take pride in quality more than quantity.

50
00:05:13.455 --> 00:05:22.328
In my village silk making is so much more than just making a profit; we view our work as a spiritual exercise.

51
00:05:22.329 --> 00:05:31.865
Whether it is collecting the cocoons, unwinding the threads, or even spinning the silk, each movement is done precisely and slowly.

52
00:05:31.866 --> 00:05:39.402
This is why the Chinese martial art tai chi chuan includes exercises from silk-reeling techniques.

53
00:05:39.403 --> 00:05:48.847
Practicing tai chi silk-reeling exercises helps a person to move slowly, smoothly, evenly, and continuously,

54
00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:53.276
and prepares the body to make gentle yet accurate movements.

55
00:05:53.277 --> 00:06:01.720
We are totally dedicated to our art, so it is not surprising that the silk from Guangdong is considered to be superior.

56
00:06:01.721 --> 00:06:07.408
Making silk is a unique tradition of my village, my people, and my country.

57
00:06:07.409 --> 00:06:15.365
I am proud it is part of my heritage and hope that one day I can learn all the skills needed to become a proficient silk worker.

58
00:06:15.366 --> 00:06:19.029
Sadly the way silk is being made is changing,

59
00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:29.225
but I hope that silk making will always be considered a noble art and that one day my children will learn it too.

